  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0152_2316ce270b05.png\" style=\"width: 254px; height: 212px;\" /></p><p>Tangent at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> will be parallel to given line</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br />Point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> lies on curve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p><p>For normal at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Slope of normal<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>(Negative inverse of slope of tangent)<br />Equation of normal :&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>26</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>"
  }
